      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To protect against supply chain volatility, ensure your Master Service Agreement includes clear force majeure clauses that specifically address global disruptions, natural disasters, or trade restrictions. You should also incorporate fixed pricing mechanisms or indexed pricing formulas for the initial contract period to shield you from sudden price spikes. Finally, demand strict capacity maintenance obligations and pre-approved supplier diversification requirements to guarantee continued availability even during crises.",
      "source": "target",
